# Soccer photo jersey backs (always)

**One silhouette.** Morocco / Spain / Cameroon / PSG cut. Recolor body / collar / cuffs / sides and print the wordmark. Solid `#000` (LED energy). No hanger on photo backs.

**Wordmark:** baked into the PNG only (country/club, never the patron name or number). Inner collar, Cameroon arch (~7° following the shoulder/neckline), ~65% width; two-word names keep the second word on the fabric. Upright condensed heat-transfer caps — not italic, not cursive. Letter height matches or is slightly larger than the CSS patron name. Spell IVORY COAST, DR CONGO, MOZAMBIQUE. Tanzania = royal blue + yellow. Ethiopia = green + white collar. Zambia = copper/orange. CSS must **not** reprint the team name on photo kits (`.soccer-jersey-team` hidden when `usePhotoBack`).

**Number overlay:** CSS only. `#displaySub.soccer-jersey-number` is horizontally center-justified on the jersey midline. Soccer numbers are **upright** condensed (not italic / not cursive). Never left- or right-bias the mark. Apply centering before Pages upload. Patron **name** is also CSS only (`#displayMain.soccer-jersey-name`), same upright condensed type.

## FIX PROMPT — CSS hanger (Image 1) vs named photo (Image 2)

If the LED shows a CSS hanger (colored blocks, hook, CSS country name clipped by the collar) while a named PNG exists, the board took `jersey-css-back`.

Execute:

1. Catalog: `defaultBackgroundUrl` = `soccer-{slug}-back-with-country.png` or `-with-club.png`, `jerseyCssBack: false`.
2. `display-app.js`: a photo URL **wins**. Ignore `jerseyCssBack=1` on the query string when that URL is set. `usePhotoBack = !!jerseyBg`.
3. Gallery / composer: mint `jerseyCssBack=0` whenever a photo URL exists. Never `=1` for photo kits.
4. Ship the PNGs on **`origin/main`** (GitHub Pages). A workspace-only file is not live.
5. Cache-bust `display-app.js` / `jersey-catalog.js` `?v=` on composer/preview pages. Xibo stays `display.html?location=` only.

## LAYOUT — Tanzania lock applied to every named photo kit (QA in silhouette before Pages)

Wordmark at inner collar; patron name and number sit **slightly below** the wordmark (more air under CAMEROON / RUSSIA / UKRAINE), still clear of each other. Photo-back CSS: name `top` ~26% (96×48 / 64×48 ~25%, 64×32 ~23%); number `top` ~47% (96×48 ~46%, 64×32 ~45%), same horizontal inset as the name for midline centering; Impact / Arial Black, tabular nums, tracking ~`-.1em`. Name max ~**9.4vh** — smaller than the PNG wordmark. Do **not** publish to `origin/main` until every photo kit is checked in the Cameroon/Morocco silhouette (no hanger, number on midline, name not kissing the wordmark or number).

